From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ucrtbase: Return the x86-64 C++ exception frame size.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

On Windows 10 x86-64, __CxxQueryExceptionSize returns 32 in both
ucrtbase and vcruntime140. Wine's UCRT returns the 16-byte size of the
exception type descriptor, while __CxxRegisterExceptionObject uses a
cxx_frame_info record with four pointers.

Return the size of that record on the measured UCRT architecture.

v2 (2026-11-21): Exclude ARM64EC explicitly after independent review.
The x86-64 code path used in the AutoCAD A/B test is the same.

diff --git a/dlls/msvcrt/except.c b/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
--- a/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
+++ b/dlls/msvcrt/except.c
@@ -814,7 +814,11 @@
  */
 unsigned int CDECL __CxxQueryExceptionSize(void)
 {
+#if _MSVCR_VER >= 140 && defined(__x86_64__) && !defined(__arm64ec__)
+    return sizeof(cxx_frame_info);
+#else
     return sizeof(cxx_exception_type);
+#endif
 }

